cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this work, please cite the Internet-Draft as below."
title: "PSEA Token Profile: An EAT Profile for Action-Bound, User-Verification-Gated Transaction-Confirmation Evidence"
abstract: >
  An Entity Attestation Token (EAT, RFC 9711) profile for action-bound,
  user-verification-gated transaction-confirmation evidence: a What-You-Sign-Is-
  What-You-Execute proof that a present, user-verified human approved a specific
  named action at the moment of execution. Self-contained and device-agnostic;
  conformance is buildable from the draft alone, with no bilateral agreement or
  vendor registry required.
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/yuthent/psea-spec"
